WEBVTT

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:33.860
<i>Mt. Fuji, the highest point in Japan,</i>

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:35.440
<i>is a mountain I aspire to climb.</i>

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:40.480
<i>I could only make it partway up this summer.</i>

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:44.290
<i>But I made the decision to take on it again.</i>

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:48.410
<i>That I'm going to stand at the 
peak of Mt. Fuji this time.</i>

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:54.050
<b>Are Hiking Shoes Really Awesome?</b>

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:56.340
So anyway, Kaede-san,

00:01:56.630 --> 00:01:59.720
I was thinking of trying 
to climb Mt. Fuji again.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:01.840
Sounds great. Good luck.

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:02.720
Thanks!

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:05.840
So would you like to go with us again?

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.780
We were thinking about going 
at the end of the month...

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.230
The end of the month?

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.730
Mt. Fuji is already off-season.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:13.230
What?

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.730
But it's still September!

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:18.110
The buses aren't in service, 
and the huts are closed.

00:02:18.310 --> 00:02:21.990
I think it might be snowing 
at the summit now.

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:23.910
Really?

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:27.420
I guess I'll have to wait 
until next spring, then.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:32.500
You know, it's in April and May that 
Mt. Fuji has the most snow on it.

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:33.080
Ack!

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:35.000
Which means...

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:36.880
It's not happening until summer.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.080
<i>Summer?!</i>

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.510
<i>A year later?</i>

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:45.030
But I finally made up my mind...

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.180
There, there.

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:49.460
In that case, is there anything I can do now?

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:51.150
Let's see...

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:52.810
You can get in shape.

00:02:53.110 --> 00:02:57.200
Carry heavy stuff, try some smaller 
mountains, stuff like that.

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.610
I see!

00:02:58.610 --> 00:03:00.260
All right. Let's do this!

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:01.040
Sure.

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:06.620
Actually, maybe you should both think 
about buying proper hiking shoes.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:08.710
Hiking shoes?

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.620
Dad was saying the same thing, too.

00:03:12.290 --> 00:03:13.900
Hiking shoes...

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.670
Will I actually need them?

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:20.470
You might as well, if you're 
going to be climbing a lot.

00:03:24.990 --> 00:03:26.010
I know!

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:27.950
Let's go buy some today!

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:29.010
Today?

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:31.480
Kaede-san, could you come 
with us after school?

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:33.100
Sounds great. Let's go.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:34.560
Okay, Aoi?

00:03:35.450 --> 00:03:38.100
I don't have a lot of money, though.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.640
Don't worry. I don't, either.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:42.360
I'll ask Dad.

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:44.750
Let's go home first and then meet up again.

00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:45.890
Okay.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.040
I hope they have some cute shoes.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:52.610
So how much should we bring?

00:03:52.610 --> 00:03:53.870
Let's see...

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.540
40,000 yen should do it.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:58.740
40,000...

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:07.480
40,000 yen?!

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.540
40,000 yen...

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:16.190
40,000 yen... 40,000 yen...

00:04:17.510 --> 00:04:21.140
If I had 40,000 in the bank...

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:27.120
I could buy autumn clothes, 
yummy food, or beads...

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:33.580
Wait!

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:39.670
Do I really need hiking shoes?

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:41.740
<b>Outdoor, Camping,
and Mountain Climbing Goods</b>

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:45.280
Look at all these shoes!

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:48.180
I don't see any cute ones, though.

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:50.170
When you buy hiking shoes,

00:04:50.170 --> 00:04:53.180
you want to choose practical 
ones over fashionable ones.

00:04:53.180 --> 00:04:54.360
Manager.

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:55.220
Hello.

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:56.460
Welcome.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:57.810
Hello.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:02.190
Believe it or not, they've gotten 
a lot more stylish than before.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:07.700
They used to be uncompromisingly 
practical and made just for dirtbags,

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:11.290
but since there are a lot of girls 
like you climbing these days,

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:13.550
they've gotten a lot nicer-looking.

00:05:13.970 --> 00:05:16.780
So, what kind of shoes are 
you looking for today?

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:18.300
They're not for me,

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.580
but these two are looking for 
their first proper hiking shoes.

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:22.930
Could you help them out?

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:23.970
We'd appreciate it!

00:05:23.970 --> 00:05:25.920
W-We would.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:29.930
There are actually several 
types of hiking shoes.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:33.950
This is good if you want to just walk 
around town or hike around Chichibu.

00:05:33.950 --> 00:05:35.920
Something like this would 
be good for Mt. Takao.

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:39.720
Where have gone climbing before?

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:40.940
Um...

00:05:40.940 --> 00:05:44.520
Mt. Tanigawa, Mt. Tsukuba 
the other day, and...

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:46.080
Oh, Mt. Fuji.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.460
Likewise.

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:50.130
Do you plan to go to all kinds 
of places in the future?

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:52.260
Yes, I hope to.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:53.990
Likewise.

00:05:54.210 --> 00:05:57.370
All right, I'd recommend 
something like this, then.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:05:59.750
Give them a feel.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:00.660
Okay.

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.790
Wow, it's pretty stiff.

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:04.880
Yeah, it's stiff.

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:09.760
The sole is made not to bend.

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:10.930
Why is that?

00:06:10.930 --> 00:06:15.210
That way, it catches firmly on the rocks.

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:16.400
It doesn't slip.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.930
But if it's soft, it bends too easily.

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:21.190
It may catch, but it'll slip right off.

00:06:21.190 --> 00:06:22.300
Oh...

00:06:22.300 --> 00:06:25.210
Would you like to try them on?

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:29.600
Wow, you measure using a computer?

00:06:29.600 --> 00:06:31.800
It's just a rough measurement, though.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:34.160
The same size shoe by the same manufacturer

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:37.520
can still be a slightly different size.

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:39.520
How's that?

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:41.880
Are your toes touching the tips?

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.100
Um...

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:45.290
I think it's good.

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:48.830
You need to leave about one 
centimeter of space in front,

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:51.120
or your toes get hit when 
you're going downhill.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:52.890
What happens if they do?

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:56.120
Your nails can crack, and you 
can end up bleeding everywhere.

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:59.840
Okay, try walking in them.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:02.350
Walk up and down that thing.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:04.110
A rock face?

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:10.980
Hey, how's it going?

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:12.950
Oh, well...

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:15.620
They're kind of awkward to walk in.

00:07:15.620 --> 00:07:19.500
Try walking with your whole foot 
rather than just your toes.

00:07:20.060 --> 00:07:21.760
They're so heavy.

00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:24.180
They're so stiff, I can't turn my ankles.

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:25.560
The soles are stiff.

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:28.040
It won't be easy to walk
like you normally do.

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:32.510
Something like this?

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.220
I made it!

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:41.280
<i>They aren't comfortable to walk in.</i>

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:43.810
<i>And for something so expensive...</i>

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:47.560
Do I really need them that much?

00:07:47.560 --> 00:07:51.260
Of course, you don't <i>need</i> them.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:54.820
People in the old days climbed 
Mt. Fuji in straw sandals, after all.

00:07:55.370 --> 00:08:00.040
Besides, do you think Kato 
Buntaro had fancy hiking shoes?

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:00.990
<i>Who?</i>

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:05.930
Why not think of them as safe 
tools rather than as shoes?

00:08:05.930 --> 00:08:07.670
Tools?

00:08:07.840 --> 00:08:09.810
Sports cars are nice, aren't they?

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:15.320
In a well-paved city, they're 
comfortable and just great.

00:08:15.320 --> 00:08:21.100
But... they're no match for an 
off-roader on a rocky mountain.

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:24.560
Whether you're playing tennis, 
dancing ballet, or anything else,

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:29.070
every sport has its own kind of shoes, right?

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.070
Don't you think it's the same 
way with mountain climbing?

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:32.570
I get it!

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:39.610
<i>But if I'm going to spend 
a lot of money on them,</i>

00:08:39.610 --> 00:08:41.360
<i>I'd rather get some cute ones—</i>

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:51.120
<i>I like these shoes!</i>

00:08:52.400 --> 00:08:54.220
Do you have these in other sizes?

00:08:54.220 --> 00:08:55.550
Sure.

00:08:55.920 --> 00:08:57.060
Just a second.

00:08:57.060 --> 00:08:57.900
Okay.

00:09:01.310 --> 00:09:05.310
Break them in well so they fit your feet.

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:06.060
Okay.

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:09.900
Also, make sure you inspect 
them before you leave.

00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.940
It would be a disaster if the sole came 
off in the mountains or something.

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:15.980
Some people fix them with wire,

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:18.360
but if you have the mind 
to carry wire with you,

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:21.460
you might as well check 
your shoes before you go.

00:09:21.890 --> 00:09:23.030
That sounds...

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:25.860
<b>Mt. Takao</b>

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:25.330
...kind of familiar.

00:09:26.090 --> 00:09:30.140
Oh, and I'll teach you how to tie your 
laces so they don't come loose.

00:09:30.710 --> 00:09:32.400
There's a trick to it?

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:34.840
Make sure you remember it.

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:40.930
<i>We decided to walk up 
Mt. Tenran on our way home.</i>

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:44.730
<i>We wanted to break in our new shoes.</i>

00:09:45.580 --> 00:09:49.340
The knot that the manager taught us...

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:50.900
There.

00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.350
That should do it.

00:09:53.210 --> 00:09:56.280
Huh? Did I mess it up somehow?

00:09:56.280 --> 00:09:57.650
Sheesh.

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:00.120
You're so clumsy.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.370
It's like this.

00:10:03.040 --> 00:10:05.570
This is a normal bow knot.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:08.720
It starts out the same,

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:15.370
but you put this loop through 
the hole a second time.

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:17.180
There. All done.

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:20.320
That'll keep it from coming loose too easily.

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:23.650
But you can untie it the same 
way you would a bow knot.

00:10:23.650 --> 00:10:24.750
Okay.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:27.350
Now...

00:10:27.630 --> 00:10:29.900
To Mt. Tenran we go!

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:44.580
Mt. Tenran Peak / Mt. Tounosu

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:44.580
Mt. Tenran Peak via rocky 
path and sixteen arhats

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:41.930
Let's go via the rocky path course.

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:43.240
Agreed.

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:55.460
They were right.

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:57.540
It's not the same.

00:11:00.820 --> 00:11:03.350
It definitely feels safer.

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:06.690
<i>They're a bit heavy and stiff, but...</i>

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:13.580
Are you okay?

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:15.320
Yeah.

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:19.030
<i>My feet are fine.</i>

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:23.140
<i>So there's a reason they're heavy and stiff.</i>

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:29.910
We made it!

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:34.300
Kaede-san, hiking shoes are nice.

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:36.540
I'm glad I took the plunge.

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:37.670
I know, right?

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:40.090
I'm glad you get it.

00:11:40.320 --> 00:11:43.720
You looked like you were upset about 
spending the money just a minute ago.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:45.100
Shut up!

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:49.400
<i>I'll use these to climb a lot of mountains,</i>

00:11:49.400 --> 00:11:51.020
<i>build up stamina,</i>

00:11:52.220 --> 00:11:55.800
<i>and take on Mt. Fuji next summer.</i>

00:11:57.220 --> 00:11:59.000
<i>To be continued.</i>

00:11:57.220 --> 00:11:59.960
<b>To Be Continued</b>
